emscripten: open every environment lock-free and written through the map.

emscripten has no process-shared mutexes (ENOTSUP), and a file mapping is
a copy, which LMDB's writes with pwrite do not reach: MDB_NOLOCK (a wasm
program is a single process) and MDB_WRITEMAP.  Also applied to the copy
bundled by the lmdb bindings (the lmdb recipe).

--- a/libraries/liblmdb/mdb.c
+++ b/libraries/liblmdb/mdb.c
@@
 mdb_env_open(MDB_env *env, const char *path, unsigned int flags, mdb_mode_t mode)
 {
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+	/* ocaml-emcc: no process-shared mutexes, and writes with pwrite do not
+	 * reach a file mapping (a copy) */
+	flags |= MDB_NOLOCK | MDB_WRITEMAP;
+#endif
